{
  "title": "Create recipes from one text box through the full backend pipeline",
  "description": "The current recipe creation UI requires too much field-by-field input and too many clicks. \
The user clarified that recipe creation should be entirely unstructured: one text box whose contents go through the normal backend flow. \
They also report that a recipe created in the UI received no ingredient weight estimates; include this as a bug to reproduce and fix in this work.\n\
\n\
Expected behavior:\n\
- Make one unstructured text box the recipe creation UI on web and iOS, supporting typing or pasting a whole recipe. \
Accept a whole recipe containing title, ingredients, instructions, and any available metadata without requiring users to split it into fields or add each ingredient separately.\n\
- Send creation through the normal backend ingestion pipeline, including ingredient parsing, supported weight estimates/conversions, and applicable enrichment. \
Do not introduce a separate lightweight text parser or save path that skips the processing normal imports receive. \
Return a structured draft that the user can review, correct, and save in a short flow.\n\
- Reproduce the reported absence of weight estimates after UI creation. \
For ingredients with supported quantities and density data, creating a recipe from text must produce the same weight estimates as the normal backend flow. \
Keep unsupported estimates explicitly unavailable rather than inventing weights.\n\
- Preserve the pasted text and edits on failure, show actionable errors, and make missing or ambiguous fields visible without inventing recipe content.\n\
- Review the surrounding creation/import flow to reduce unnecessary clicks; adding another buried control to the existing form is insufficient.\n\
\n\
Validation: Add API end-to-end tests before connecting any new endpoint to either UI. \
Cover representative pasted recipes, incomplete input, and pipeline failures, plus the paste/review/save flow on both clients. \
Add regression coverage that UI-created recipes receive expected ingredient weight estimates and follow the same backend processing as imports. \
Run make pipeline for extraction/parsing changes and commit intentional data/ diffs. \
Keep parsing logic on the server; follow doc/client-logic-sharing.md for any duplicated deterministic client logic.",
